===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|twerc}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|twerc}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*dwergaz}}. The development Middle High German ''tw-'' > modern German ''zw-'' is regular. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|dwerg}}, English {{m|en|dwarf}}, Danish {{m|da|dværg}}.

